, 33b:4-6, the Samaritans' addition conceded and refuted), two mounds by the Jordan opposite Gilgal (R. Elazar — 33b:7-9; 27:4 the same day), A ROUTE, NOT A PLACE (R. Eliezer ben Yaakov — 33b:10: the way, the settled, the plain — as the cloud showed the way the first time): gerizim_ebal_place; THE MIRACLES OF THE DAY — sixty mil (a mile) and no man stood before them, 'I will send My terror before you' (Exodus 23:27 — Tosefta Sotah 8:6: 11:25's receipt pointed at 23:27 a second time after the Sifrei 52:4); the dispossession the crossing's condition (Tosefta Sotah 8:3); Gilgal the Torah's one seat; Moreh's terebinths Abram's (Genesis 12:6 — journeyed 'the place of Shechem' on the tape)
